You grade 3 answers to one task about a git repository.
For each criterion listed and each answer, decide pass (true) or fail (false) and give a one-line reason.
Use the ground truth for every number. A criterion that asks for a hedge passes only when the answer hedges.
Reply with ONLY a JSON object: {"A": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "B": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "C": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}]}
with one entry per listed criterion, using its number n (1, 2, 3, 4).

TASK PROMPT:
Who actually owns the code in this repo? I want to know whose code is still here today, not who has made the most commits.

