FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Most surviving code traces to two people, Doug (`<email redacted>`) and Troy Goode (`<email redacted>`). Neither has committed since 2021 and 2019, so their code is mostly orphaned. The one person who looks like the biggest owner by raw blame, `fiona@formatter.example`, got there with one bulk reformat commit.

**The reformat distorts the numbers.** Commit `62628c0` (fiona, 2026-04-12, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") rewrote 1,016 lines across 4 files. Plain `git blame` on HEAD credits it, so fiona shows 1,016 surviving lines. With `git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0`, the ranking changes:

| Author | Surviving lines (raw) | Surviving lines (ignoring reformat) | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| fiona | 1,016 | 237 | 2026-04-12 |
| doug | 260 | 564 | 2021-09-07 |
| troygoode | 224 | 595 | 2019-05-27 |
| inigomarquinez | 94 | 94 | 2024-05-14 |
| jonchurch | 72 | 72 | 2026-01-16 |
| bjohansebas | 67 | 67 | 2025-07-23 |
| ignaciomangas | 54 | 54 | 2025-12-01 |
| ulisesgascongonzalez | 52 | 52 | 2026-01-22 |
| troy@laptop.example | 37 | 47 | 2026-04-10 |

**Per area** (ignoring the reformat; "active" = committed since 2025-04-12, 12 months before the newest commit):

| Zone | Main surviving owners | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` | troygoode 98, fiona 57, doug 36 | Spread across people. Active share depends on whether troy@laptop is the same person as troygoode (see below). |
| `test/test.js` | doug 270, troygoode 213, fiona 178 | Spread. Doug and troygoode are inactive. Fiona is the only active major owner. |
| `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `README.md` | troygoode dominant | Orphaned if troygoode is inactive. README's second owner (jonchurch) is active. |
| `test/vary.js` | troy@laptop 36/36 | **Bus factor 1** (one active person, sole author). |
| `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` | bjohansebas 63/66 | **Bus factor 1**. Active only under the 2025-04 cutoff; see sensitivity below. |
| `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` | inigomarquinez 68/73 | **Orphaned**. Last commit 2024-05. |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | doug 108, ignaciomangas 54, ulisesgascongonzalez 30, inigomarquinez 26 | Mixed. Doug and inigo inactive; ignacio and ulises active. |
| `.github/dependabot.yml` | ulisesgascongonzalez 15/15 | **Bus factor 1**, active. |
| `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml`, `.gitignore`, `test/support/env.js`, `LICENSE`, `HISTORY.md` | doug, nearly all | **Orphaned**. |
| `package.json` | doug 20, troygoode 12, bjohansebas 4 | Mostly orphaned. |

**Orphaned** = no active author holds the majority of the surviving lines. **Bus factor 1** = one active author holds it. These are different risks; the table keeps them separate.

**Caveats:**
- **Identity:** `troy@laptop.example` committed on 2026-04-10 under the name "Troy Goode", which probably matches `<email redacted>`. I did not merge them. If they are the same person, troygoode is active and `lib/index.js` and the test files are not orphaned. Please confirm.
- **Activity cutoff:** I used the repo's newest commit (2026-04-12) as "now". If you measure from today (2026-10-23), bjohansebas (last 2025-07) drops out, and `codeql.yml` becomes orphaned.
- **The script:** I ran `ownership.mjs --dry-run --no-github`, so it wrote nothing into the repo. Its CODEOWNERS named fiona as the `*` fallback owner. That is driven by the reformat commit and should not be used as-is. The script weights commits by age, not surviving lines, so I used blame for the numbers above.
- **Identity mapping:** No GitHub logins were resolved, so everything is by email.

I haven't written a CODEOWNERS file or an HTML report. If you want either, I can generate them, or add the reformat commit to a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file so future blame stays accurate.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | wc -l && git ls-files -z | xargs -0 file --mime-type | grep -v 'image/\|font/\|binary' | cut -d: -f1 | wc -l
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | xargs -0 file --mime-type | grep -v 'image/\|font/\|binary' | cut -d: -f1 | tr '\n' '\0' | xargs -0 git blame -w -e --line-porcelain HEAD -- 2>/dev/null | awk '/^author-mail /{m=$0} /^\t/{ if (m!="") {c[m]++; m=""} } END{for(k in c) print c[k], k}' | sort -rn | head -30
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | xargs -0 file --mime-type | grep -v 'image/\|font/\|binary' | cut -d: -f1 > /tmp/textfiles.txt; while IFS= read -r f; do git blame -w -e --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null; done < /tmp/textfiles.txt | awk '/^author-mail /{m=$0} /^\t/{ if (m!="") {c[m]++; m=""} } END{for(k in c) print c[k], k}' | sort -rn | head -30; echo ---; while IFS= read -r f; do echo "$f"; done < /tmp/textfiles.txt | head -30
 - Bash: git show -s --format='%h %an <%ae> %ad %s' 62628c0 b2005d9 02afce3; echo ---; while IFS= read -r f; do git blame -w --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null; done < /tmp/textfiles.txt | awk '/^[0-9a-f]{40} /{h=substr($1,1,7)} /^\t/{c[h]++} END{for(k in c) print c[k], k}' | sort -rn | head -8; echo ---; git remote -v; git log --format='%an' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3
 - Bash: while IFS= read -r f; do git blame -w -e --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null; done < /tmp/textfiles.txt | awk '/^author-mail /{m=$0} /^\t/{t++; if(m!=""){c[m]++; m=""}} END{print "total", t; for(k in c) print c[k], k}' | sort -rn | head -4; git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -5
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own most of the surviving code. Fiona Formatter's share is large but mostly mechanical.

Surviving lines by `git blame` at HEAD, across the 18 tracked text files. The total is roughly 2,500 lines, so these shares are approximate:

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (`<email redacted>` + `troy@laptop.example`) | ~650 | ~25% | Two emails, combined here. Largest single owner. |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson (`<email redacted>`) | 470 | ~19% | Second-largest owner. |
| Fiona Formatter (`fiona@formatter.example`) | 291 | ~12% | Almost all from one commit, `62628c0` ("reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"). |
| Everyone else | ~1,100 | ~45% | Long tail, e.g. `inigomarquinez` 95, `<email redacted>` 72, `bjohansebas` 67. |

Caveats:
- **Fiona's share is a reformat, not authorship.** Her commit rewrote indentation and quotes across the JS, so blame credits her for lines whose logic someone else wrote. The original authors of those lines are hidden. Troy and Doug are probably understated, but I can't quantify by how much without re-blaming past `62628c0`.
- **`-w` ignores whitespace only.** Quote changes still count as edits, so the reformat share is partly reattributed.
- **Blame measures who last touched a line, not who designed it.** Use it as a rough ownership signal, not a credit list.

If you want the reformat ignored, I can re-run blame with `git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0` and show the adjusted numbers.

